    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "> Add more document on these;\r\n\r\nSure. \r\n\r\n> Add one option so that Triton can use fast math instructions automatically without changing user code;\r\n\r\n(1) We have already incorporated fast math into specific code paths, such as exp, but cos and sin use the slower path by default (verification required).\r\n(2) It might be beneficial to provide users with detailed control over each function. It's worth noting that '--use_fast_math' is an NVCC option, but not a ptxas option, which implies '--ftz=true --prec-div=false --prec-sqrt=false --fmad=true'. Essentially, this only influences the ftz modifier, div instruction, and sqrt instruction for now, which I believe is not unattainable from the user's perspective. If not, the codegen portion for each operation would need to be altered to achieve this.\r\n\r\n**With that being said, I think it's a valid concern to define a \"TRITON_USE_FAST_MATH\" option.**. However, it's not clear to me what should be enabled in the fast math mode and what shouldn't. I would probably want to see a clear picture or a RFC about it. ",
